[# docs-src/repos/cx-platform-sso.cxd — the sign-on repository's page,
   repo-cx-platform-sso.html (RULED: DOCS-41, DOCS-47, DOCS-49 wave 3).
   Facts from the registries; the one example from its own corpus (the sso
   suite). #]

[repo name=cx-platform-sso
  [intro
    """The receiving half of enterprise sign-on, as request in and
       response out. `cx-platform-sso` is a deployment's OpenID Connect
       relying party, its SAML service provider, its SCIM provisioning
       routes, its logout channels and its token endpoint — each a verb from
       a `[request]` value to a `[response]` value, with the session it
       establishes held by the identity repository and its state in the
       store."""]
  [body
    """A login begins by checking the requested return-to against the
       allow-list — an absolute URL, a protocol-relative one or one carrying
       a newline is refused before anything is parked — then generates
       state, nonce and the PKCE verifier together, parks them, and answers
       a 302 to the provider's authorize endpoint. Nothing dials. The
       callback treats a missing state, a state never issued, a replayed
       state and an expired row as one refusal, deliberately, so an attacker
       learns nothing from which one they hit."""]
  [body
    """The SAML assertion consumer refuses a GET, a body with no response, a
       response that is not base64 and an oversized body before it decodes
       anything, and a real signed assertion establishes a real session;
       the metadata endpoint answers the service provider descriptor
       verbatim. SCIM refuses a wrong bearer, a missing one and a prefix of
       the right one alike, and no configured token is not an open door;
       create, read, patch and delete round-trip through the store. The
       token endpoint serves client credentials and no other grant. The
       repository's `examples/` directory carries the interop tests a
       deployment is graded against."""]
  [gives
    """One module of the platform group, a pure-CX package over the codecs
       the language ships — `oidc`, `saml`, `scim`, `url`, `http-client` —
       linking to the reference page projected from its own
       documentation."""]
  [try
    """The classic sign-on defect, refused: a login link carrying an absolute
       `return-to` would send a freshly authenticated user, cookie in hand,
       to someone else's page. The response's body is an error value with
       its own code, answered before anything is parked — and the program
       reads it as a value, no grant, no socket."""]
  [fixture id=sso-001-login-refuses-an-absolute-return-to]
  [status
    """Sign-on ships as a package: its module is bundled into the build from
       the pin, the first repository to leave the front door, and the
       interop tests run from its own tree."""]]
